{"reference":"1 Kings 16","book":"1 Kings","chapter":16,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Ahab Beyond This Chapter","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter ends by introducing Ahab. An external monument, the Kurkh Monolith, names Ahab in a coalition at Qarqar, an event not narrated in 1 Kings. This independently places an Israelite king within ninth-century regional politics, though it does not establish every detail or theological claim made in the book.","verse_refs":["1 Kings 17:1-24","1 Kings 18:1-46","1 Kings 19:1-21","1 Kings 20:1-43","1 Kings 21:1-29","1 Kings 22:1-40"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_016_d06dc5caca479dfdb99f21c6"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"inference"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}